%% Reader question: How does a learning become a consumable constraint without assuming instant fleet-wide propagation?
%% Evidence cutoff: 2026-07-11
%% Claim status: reference design; public distribution mechanics are verified, private adoption is not publicly reproducible
flowchart TB
    accTitle: Skill and knowledge propagation
    accDescr: A learning becomes a candidate, is classified and reviewed, then released as a versioned local, internal, or public artifact. Each consumer adopts the version through a reviewed change and supplies loading and outcome evidence. A separate upstream path reviews and pins an existing public artifact instead of copying it.

    O["Failure, friction, or useful observation"] --> C["Candidate learning with source and cutoff"]
    C --> K{"Knowledge to read or capability to call?"}
    K -->|"Knowledge"| G["Generalize procedure and remove private context"]
    K -->|"Capability"| T["Specify a narrow typed tool boundary"]

    G --> A{"Intended audience?"}
    A -->|"One role"| L["Agent-local candidate"]
    A -->|"Several trusted roles"| I["Internal-fleet candidate"]
    A -->|"General public"| P["Public-fleet candidate"]

    L --> R["Behavior examples, review, and version"]
    I --> R
    P --> R
    T --> R

    N["Need already served upstream?"] --> U["Review provenance, license, security, and utility"]
    U --> V["Pin curated upstream version"]

    R --> V2["Release versioned artifact"]
    V --> D["Consumer upgrade through reviewable change"]
    V2 --> D
    D --> E["Evidence that consumer loaded or invoked it"]
    E --> M["Measure recurrence, outcome, and steering cost"]
    M -->|"Useful"| Q["Keep, refine, or promote"]
    M -->|"No demonstrated value"| X["Narrow, deprecate, or delete"]
    Q --> C
